{"id":"mahabharata-1-196","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":196,"title":"षण्णवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 196 · Drona agrees with Bhishma; Karna objects","summary":{"en":"Drona supports Bhishma, advising that the Pandavas be invited back with honour and given their share. Karna accuses the counsellors of disloyalty, and Drona warns that if his advice is ignored the Kurus will soon perish.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಗೌರವದಿಂದ ಮರಳಿ ಕರೆದು ಅವರ ಪಾಲು ಕೊಡಬೇಕೆಂದು ದ್ರೋಣನು ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಬೆಂಬಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕರ್ಣನು ಸಲಹೆಗಾರರನ್ನು ದ್ರೋಹಿಗಳೆಂದು ಆರೋಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನ್ನ ಸಲಹೆ ತಿರಸ್ಕರಿಸಿದರೆ ಕುರುಗಳು ಬೇಗ ನಾಶವಾಗುವರೆಂದು ದ್ರೋಣನು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रोण भीष्म का समर्थन करते हुए सलाह देते हैं कि पाण्डवों को सम्मान से वापस बुलाकर उनका भाग दिया जाए। कर्ण सलाहकारों पर निष्ठाहीनता का आरोप लगाते हैं, और द्रोण चेतावनी देते हैं कि उनकी सलाह न मानी गई तो कुरु शीघ्र नष्ट होंगे।","te":"పాండవులను గౌరవంగా తిరిగి పిలిచి వారి భాగం ఇవ్వాలని ద్రోణుడు భీష్ముని సమర్థిస్తాడు. సలహాదారులపై కర్ణుడు ద్రోహ నేరం మోపుతాడు; తన సలహా పెడచెవిన పెడితే కురువులు త్వరలోనే నశిస్తారని ద్రోణుడు హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்களை மரியாதையுடன் திரும்ப அழைத்து அவர்கள் பங்கைக் கொடுக்க வேண்டும் என்று துரோணர் பீஷ்மரை ஆதரிக்கிறார். ஆலோசகர்கள் விசுவாசமற்றவர்கள் என்று கர்ணன் குற்றம் சாட்ட, தம் அறிவுரை புறக்கணிக்கப்பட்டால் குருக்கள் விரைவில் அழிவர் என்று துரோணர் எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"ഭീഷ്മരെ ദ്രോണർ പിന്തുണയ്ക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരെ ബഹുമാനത്തോടെ തിരിച്ചുവിളിച്ച്, അവർക്ക് അവകാശപ്പെട്ടത് നൽകണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു. ഉപദേശകർ വഞ്ചകരാണെന്ന് കർണ്ണൻ ആരോപിക്കുന്നു; തന്റെ ഉപദേശം അവഗണിച്ചാൽ കൗരവർ ഉടൻ നശിക്കുമെന്ന് ദ്രോണർ മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.196; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"विदुरागमनपर्व","titleEn":"Viduragamana Parva (Vidura's coming)","verses":[{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मन्त्राय समुपानीतैर्धृतराष्ट्रहितैर्नृप ।\nधर्म्यं पथ्यं यशस्यं च वाच्यमित्यनुशुश्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that those brought to counsel who wish Dhritarashtra well, king, must speak what is righteous, beneficial and renowned."}},{"n":2,"text":"ममाप्येषा मतिस्तात या भीष्मस्य महात्मनः ।\nसंविभज्यास्तु कौन्तेया धर्म एष सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My view too, child, is that of the great-souled Bhishma: the sons of Kunti should be given their share. This is eternal dharma."}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रेष्यतां द्रुपदायाशु नरः कश्चित्प्रियंवदः ।\nबहुलं रत्नमादाय तेषामर्थाय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let some pleasant-spoken man be sent quickly to Drupada, Bharata, with many jewels for the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"मिथः कृत्यं च तस्मै स आदाय बहु गच्छतु ।\nवृद्धिं च परमां ब्रूयात्तत्संयोगोद्भवां तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let him go taking much for Drupada and for the private business between them, and let him speak of the great gain that has come from this union."}},{"n":5,"text":"संप्रीयमाणं त्वां ब्रूयाद्राजन्दुर्योधनं तथा ।\nअसकृद्द्रुपदे चैव धृष्टद्युम्ने च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let him say to Drupada, and repeatedly to Dhrishtadyumna, king, that you and Duryodhana are well pleased."}},{"n":6,"text":"उचितत्वं प्रियत्वं च योगस्यापि च वर्णयेत् ।\nपुनः पुनश्च कौन्तेयान्माद्रीपुत्रौ च सान्त्वयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let him describe the fitness and the pleasantness of the alliance, and again and again console the sons of Kunti and the two sons of Madri."}},{"n":7,"text":"हिरण्मयानि शुभ्राणि बहून्याभरणानि च ।\nवचनात्तव राजेन्द्र द्रौपद्याः संप्रयच्छतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"At your word, king of kings, let him present to Draupadi many bright golden ornaments."}},{"n":8,"text":"तथा द्रुपदपुत्राणां सर्वेषां भरतर्षभ ।\nपाण्डवानां च सर्वेषां कुन्त्या युक्तानि यानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise to all of Drupada's sons, bull of the Bharatas, and to all the Pandavas and to Kunti, whatever is fitting."}},{"n":9,"text":"एवं सान्त्वसमायुक्तं द्रुपदं पाण्डवैः सह ।\nउक्त्वाथानन्तरं ब्रूयात्तेषामागमनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus in conciliatory terms to Drupada and the Pandavas, let him then speak about their coming here."}},{"n":10,"text":"अनुज्ञातेषु वीरेषु बलं गच्छतु शोभनम् ।\nदुःशासनो विकर्णश्च पाण्डवानानयन्त्विह ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the heroes have given their consent, let a fine force go, and let Duhshasana and Vikarna bring the Pandavas here."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततस्ते पार्थिवश्रेष्ठ पूज्यमानाः सदा त्वया ।\nप्रकृतीनामनुमते पदे स्थास्यन्ति पैतृके ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of kings, always honoured by you, they will take their place in their father's seat with the approval of the people."}},{"n":12,"text":"एवं तव महाराज तेषु पुत्रेषु चैव ह ।\nवृत्तमौपयिकं मन्ये भीष्मेण सह भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, great king, together with Bhishma, I think this course is the proper one for you and for those sons of yours, Bharata."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"योजितावर्थमानाभ्यां सर्वकार्येष्वनन्तरौ ।\nन मन्त्रयेतां त्वच्छ्रेयः किमद्भुततरं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These two, who are always engaged by you with wealth and honour in every matter, give you no good counsel; what could be more astonishing?"}},{"n":14,"text":"दुष्टेन मनसा यो वै प्रच्छन्नेनान्तरात्मना ।\nब्रूयान्निःश्रेयसं नाम कथं कुर्यात्सतां मतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could one who speaks of what is best with a wicked mind and a hidden inner purpose do what the good approve?"}},{"n":15,"text":"न मित्राण्यर्थकृच्छ्रेषु श्रेयसे वेतराय वा ।\nविधिपूर्वं हि सर्वस्य दुःखं वा यदि वा सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friends do not decide in times of need whether it is for good or ill; for everyone, pain or pleasure comes by ordained destiny."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृतप्रज्ञोऽकृतप्रज्ञो बालो वृद्धश्च मानवः ।\nससहायोऽसहायश्च सर्वं सर्वत्र विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether wise or unwise, child or old, with helpers or without, a man everywhere gets whatever is his lot."}},{"n":17,"text":"श्रूयते हि पुरा कश्चिदम्बुवीच इति श्रुतः ।\nआसीद्राजगृहे राजा मागधानां महीक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is told that long ago there was a king called Ambuvicha in Rajagriha, king of the rulers of the Magadhas."}},{"n":18,"text":"स हीनः करणैः सर्वैरुच्छ्वासपरमो नृपः ।\nअमात्यसंस्थः कार्येषु सर्वेष्वेवाभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king, deprived of all his faculties and with only breath left, then depended on his minister in all affairs."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्यामात्यो महाकर्णिर्बभूवैकेश्वरः पुरा ।\nस लब्धबलमात्मानं मन्यमानोऽवमन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"His minister was Mahakarni, who in those days was sole master. Believing himself powerful, he despised the king."}},{"n":20,"text":"स राज्ञ उपभोग्यानि स्त्रियो रत्नधनानि च ।\nआददे सर्वशो मूढ ऐश्वर्यं च स्वयं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That fool took for himself everything the king would have enjoyed: women, jewels and wealth, and the sovereignty itself."}},{"n":21,"text":"तदादाय च लुब्धस्य लाभाल्लोभो व्यवर्धत ।\nतथा हि सर्वमादाय राज्यमस्य जिहीर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having taken it, his greed grew with gain, for in the same way he sought to take the kingdom itself away from him."}},{"n":22,"text":"हीनस्य करणैः सर्वैरुच्छ्वासपरमस्य च ।\nयतमानोऽपि तद्राज्यं न शशाकेति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that though he tried, he could not take the kingdom from one who was deprived of all faculties and had only breath left."}},{"n":23,"text":"किमन्यद्विहितान्नूनं तस्य सा पुरुषेन्द्रता ।\nयदि ते विहितं राज्यं भविष्यति विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"What else but ordained fate could keep such kingship with him? If the kingdom is ordained for you, lord of the people,"}},{"n":24,"text":"मिषतः सर्वलोकस्य स्थास्यते त्वयि तद्ध्रुवम् ।\nअतोऽन्यथा चेद्विहितं यतमानो न लप्स्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"it will surely stay with you before the eyes of all the world. If it is ordained otherwise, you will not get it however you try."}},{"n":25,"text":"एवं विद्वन्नुपादत्स्व मन्त्रिणां साध्वसाधुताम् ।\nदुष्टानां चैव बोद्धव्यमदुष्टानां च भाषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing this, wise one, take note of the goodness or badness of counsellors, and of what the wicked and the not-wicked say."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"विद्म ते भावदोषेण यदर्थमिदमुच्यते ।\nदुष्टः पाण्डवहेतोस्त्वं दोषं ख्यापयसे हि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We know, from the fault in your intention, why this is said: you are wicked, and for the Pandavas' sake you proclaim a fault in us."}},{"n":27,"text":"हितं तु परमं कर्ण ब्रवीमि कुरुवर्धनम् ।\nअथ त्वं मन्यसे दुष्टं ब्रूहि यत्परमं हितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, I am telling you what is supremely beneficial and makes the Kurus prosper. If you think it is bad, then say what is the highest good."}},{"n":28,"text":"अतोऽन्यथा चेत्क्रियते यद्ब्रवीमि परं हितम् ।\nकुरवो विनशिष्यन्ति नचिरेणेति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If it is done otherwise than what I tell you for the highest good, I believe the Kurus will perish before long."}}]}]}